  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale**  \n   We propose to use a hierarchical Bayesian optimization framework combined with multi-resolution \n   expansion of the candidate solution. The key differences are:  \n   - Instead of purely gradient-based optimization, we combine local refinement (gradient-based) with \n     global exploration (Bayesian optimization)  \n   - We introduce a new hierarchical representation: coarse-resolution \"skeleton\" with adaptive refinement  \n   - Use exponential tilts for better gradient estimation and constraint handling  \n   Bottlenecks addressed:  \n     * Current parent algorithm may get stuck in local optima due to gradient smoothing deficiencies  \n     * Adaptive hyperparameter tuning is not systematic  \n\n2. **Mathematical specification**  \n   **Variables**:  \n   - Base solution \\(h_{base} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{9} \\sim initial\\_h\\_values\\) (given)  \n   - Coarse-to-fine hierarchy: \\(h_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n_i}\\) where \\(n_i < n_j\\) for \\(i < j\\)  \n   - Exponential tilting variables \\(\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}^+\\) for improved gradient estimation  \n   - L1/2 regularization variables \\(\\lambda > 0\\) (adaptive)  \n   - Integral constraint: \\(\\sum h_i = n_i / 2\\)  \n\n   **Objective**:  \n   \\[\n   C_5 = \\max_k \\frac{1}{n_i} \\sum_{m=0}^{n_i-1-k} h_i[m] \\cdot (1 - h_i[m+k])\n   \\]  \n   Minimize \\(C_5\\) (lower is better)  \n\n   **Constraints**:  \n   \\[\n   0 \\leq h_i[j] \\leq 1, \\forall j; \\quad \\sum_j h_i[j] = n_i / 2\n   \\]  \n\n   **Gradient estimation**:  \n   \\[\n   \\nabla_{h_i} C_5 \\approx \\frac{ \\text{overlap}(h_i + \\epsilon s) - \\text{overlap}(h_i - \\epsilon s) }{2\\epsilon s} \n   \\]  \n   where \\(\\epsilon\\) is perturbation, \\(s\\) is unit vector direction  \n\n   **3. Implementation procedure**  \n   **Stage 1: Global exploration**  \n   - Input: \\(h_{base}\\) (15 points), initial alpha \\(= 10\\), maxevals = 50  \n   - Execute Bayesian optimization (OptL-BFGS-B) with:  \n     * Exponential constraint projection: \\(\\Pi_{\\text{simplex}}(h) = \\frac{h}{\\sum h} \\cdot \\frac{\\text{target}}{\\text{actual}}\\)  \n     * Dynamic alpha adjustment: \\(\\alpha \\leftarrow 10^{\\max(4, \\text{iteration}}}\\)  \n     * Perturbation strategies:  \n       1. Random flip: replace 10% of h with [0,1]  \n       2. Rescaling: \\(h \\leftarrow h / \\mu + \\sigma \\cdot \\text{randn}\\)  \n       3. Iterative smoothing: apply exponential tilt for 5 steps  \n\n   **Stage 2: Multi-resolution expansion**  \n   - Coarsely control resolution hierarchy: [15, 33, 55, 99, 175, 289, 425]  \n   - Ascending resolution loop:  \n     * Evaluate candidate on grid \\(n\\)\n     * Refine using BiCGSTAB spectral gradient method  \n     * Project integral constraint with weighted $$ projection  \n   - Bounding box indices updated:  \n     \\[\n     \\mathcal{I}_{\\min} = \\min_{j}(h) \\cdot 0.8, \\quad \\mathcal{I}_{\\max} = \\max_{j}(h) \\cdot 1.2  \n     \\]  \n\n   **Stage 3: Final polishing**  \n   - Use adaptive line search with:  \n     \\[\n     h_{\\text{new}} = h_{\\text{old}} + \\tau \\cdot (h_{\\text{explore}} - h_{\\text{exploit}})\n     \\]\n   - Entropy pruning: remove candidates with low Shannon entropy, \\(\\sum -h \\log h \\leq 1.5\\)  \n   - Early termination: if consecutive evaluations stabilize \\|\\|\u2207f\\|\\| < 1e-5  \n\n   **4. Search choices and variations**  \n   - **Perturbation strategies**:  \n     1. Spatially correlated noise: covariance \\(\\kappa(x,y) = \\exp(-|x-y|/\\theta)\\)  \n     2. Periodic initialization: trial \\(h_j[x] \\leftarrow \\sin(x + \\varphi_j)\\)  \n     3. Shuffling-based: order permutation of positions  \n   - **Adaptive hyperparameter tuning**:  \n     * Learning rate: \\(10^{4-q}\\), \\(q = \\emptyset\\) based on iteration count\n     * Penalty weight: \\(\\lambda = 0.5 + 0.001 \\cdot \\text{iterations}\\)\n     * Epsilon target: \\(\\epsilon_{\\text{target}} \\leftarrow 1e3 / \\text{n\\_points}\\)\n\n   **5. Compute budget and robustness**  \n   - Estimated runtime: 1200s (timer budget accounted)\n   * Resolution-specific allocation:  \n     Base resolution spends $\\leq 20s$, each finer stage +25% time  \n   - Fallback procedure:  \n     1. If candidate violates box constraint, apply $\\mathcal{I}_{\\min}/\\mathcal{I}_{\\max}}$ clipping  \n     2. Compute redundancy factor: $r = \\|h_{\\text{new}} - h_{\\text{old}}\\|_1 / \\|h_{\\text{old}}\\|$  \n        * $r < 0.05$: abandon candidate if plateau observed  \n   - Complexity: $O(n^2)$ due to full correlation at every step  \n\n   **6. Validation and return contract**  \n   - Requirements checking:  \n     1. Integral: $\\left| \\sum h_i - n_i/2 \\right| \\leq 1e-6$  \n     2. Bounded: $0 \\leq h_i[j] \\leq 1 \\forall j$  \n     3. Score validity: $C_5 = \\frac{1}{n_i} \\cdot \\text{final correlation max}$  \n   - Objective evaluation:  \n     \\begin{align*}\n        &\\text{overlap}_k = \\sum_{m=0}^{n_i-1-k} h_i[m] \\cdot \\text{clip}(1-h_i[m+k], 0,1) \\\\\n        &C_5 = \\max_k \\text{overlap}_k / n_i\n     \\end{align*}  \n   - Fallback solution: return parent $(initial\\_h, C_{parent}, n=425)$ if adaptive fails",
